  "body": "Two debug tests on `testdata/models/solidcraft_for_beginners.sc` exceeded 60 s in the post-merge batch gate (`3a240b7fb`):\n- `kernel suites: machining_mesh` took 66 s on the post-merge runner. `solidcraft_sample_meshes_within_the_app_chord` (`crates/kernel/tests/machining_mesh.rs:29`) took 128.7 s locally in debug. It meshes the full Solidcraft sample at `TOL = 0.005` mm and triggers a `0.0025` mm replan.\n- `ui suites: lib` took 142 s on the post-merge runner. `launch_file_tests::a_solidcraft_design_is_imported` imports the full Solidcraft sample in debug inside the exclusive UI lane.\n\nBoth tests exceed the 60 s debug limit in `AGENTS.md` (\"Testing\").\nEvery UI step runs alone in batch and release gates. Extra seconds in `ui suites: lib` add directly to gate wall time.\n\nWhat to do:\n1. Move `solidcraft_sample_meshes_within_the_app_chord` in `crates/kernel/tests/machining_mesh.rs:29` to `#[ignore = \"heavy lane: ...\"]`.\n2. Keep a fast debug test in `machining_mesh.rs` that checks the machining-mesh contract under 10 s.\n3. Update `launch_file_tests::a_solidcraft_design_is_imported` in `crates/ui` to use a small `.sc` fixture, or move the full-sample import to the release heavy lane.\n4. Keep every import, UI state, and refusal assertion.\n5. Keep the `#[test]` count of `camcraft-kernel` and `camcraft-ui` equal or higher.\n\nDone means:\n- Neither `kernel suites: machining_mesh` nor `ui suites: lib` has an active debug test over 60 s.\n- The full-chord Solidcraft assertions still run and pass in release `--ignored`.\n- The `#[test]` count of both crates stays equal or higher.\n\nPart of #2556\n",
